WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.200
MyCampusView Academy. Robotics 101, video 4: How an IR sensor sees the line.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.135
How can a robot see a black line?

3
00:00:08.185 --> 00:00:12.239
It uses invisible light called infrared.

4
00:00:12.289 --> 00:00:16.650
Your TV remote uses the same kind of light.

5
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.912
Each sensor module has two small parts.

6
00:00:20.962 --> 00:00:26.265
One is an infrared light, which shines down at the floor.

7
00:00:26.315 --> 00:00:32.650
The other is a receiver, which measures how much light bounces back.

8
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.488
Over a white floor, most of the light bounces back.

9
00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:44.650
The receiver sees a lot of light, so the sensor says: white.

10
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:51.650
Over a black line, the black surface soaks up most of the light.

11
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:56.650
Very little comes back, so the sensor says: black.

12
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:04.019
The module turns this into a simple digital signal, either HIGH or LOW.

13
00:01:04.069 --> 00:01:09.167
On many modules, black gives HIGH and white gives LOW.

14
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:15.650
Some are the other way round, so you will test yours in lesson nine.

15
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.461
Each module has a small blue knob.

16
00:01:19.511 --> 00:01:24.183
Turning it changes how much light counts as white.

17
00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:30.322
Hold the sensor about five to ten millimetres above the floor and

18
00:01:30.372 --> 00:01:36.178
turn the knob until the LED changes exactly when you cross the

19
00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:36.650
line.

20
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:43.332
Our robot uses two sensors, one either side of the line.

21
00:01:43.382 --> 00:01:49.088
When both see white, the line is safely between them.

22
00:01:49.138 --> 00:01:53.650
Watch the sensor dots as the robot drives.

23
00:01:54.300 --> 00:02:00.500
Next: How motors and the motor driver work.
